.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Ernst Ising (1925) solved the chain of spins s_i=\pm1 with nearest-neighbor coupling J and found no spontaneous magnetization at any temperature above zero. Ising1D solves it with the 2x2 transfer matrix, whose eigenvalues \lambda_\pm give Z_N=\lambda_+^N+\lambda_-^N exactly. The plots show a checked partition function, a magnetization that is a smooth function of field at every temperature (it only becomes a step at T=0), a correlation length that grows as e^{2J/k_BT} but stays finite, and a smooth heat-capacity maximum instead of a singularity.">

